lity. It provides categorical insights into the spatial accessibility value for modeling.\\ndf[\'Horizontal_Hydrology_Binned\'] = pd.cut(df[\'Horizontal_Distance_To_Hydrology\'], bins=3, labels=[\'Near\', \'Medium\', \'Far\'])\\ndf[\'Horizontal_Roadways_Binned\'] = pd.cut(df[\'Horizontal_Distance_To_Roadways\'], bins=3, labels=[\'Near\', \'Medium\', \'Far\'])\\ndf[\'Vertical_Hydrology_Binned\'] = pd.cut(df[\'Vertical_Distance_To_Hydrology\'], bins=3, labels=[\'Near\', \'Medium\', \'Far\'])"]': 0.0}, {'["# Hydrology_Euclidean_Distance\\n# Feature description: Compute the Euclidean distance to the nearest hydrological feature using horizontal and vertical distances.\\n# Usefulness: This feature represents the shortest physical distance to water sources, which is critical in determining soil moisture and vegetation patterns, influencing forest cover type.\\ndf[\'Hydrology_Euclidean_Distance\'] = np.sqrt(df[\'Horizontal_Distance_To_Hydrology\']2 + df[\'Vertical_Distance_To_Hydrology\']2)\\n\\n# Hillshade_Amplitude\\n# Feature description: Calculate the amplitude (max - min) across all three Hillshade values: 9am, noon, and 3pm.\\n# Usefulness: The amplitude measures variations in light exposure due to terrain shape during the day, reflecting differences in microclimates that influence vegetation types.\\ndf[\'Hillshade_Amplitude\'] = df[[\'Hillshade_9am\', \'Hillshade_Noon\', \'Hillshade_3pm\']].max(axis=1) - df[[\'Hillshade_9am\', \'Hillshade_Noon\', \'Hillshade_3pm\']].min(axis=1)\\n\\n# Road_Hydrology_Distance_Difference\\n# Feature description: Calculate the difference between Horizontal_Distance_To_Roadways and Horizontal_Distance_To_Hydrology.\\n# Usefulness: This feature captures the spatial difference between roadways and water sources, which could indicate human impact on regions near water. Proximity to water relative to roads might affect forest types.\\ndf[\'Road_Hydrology_Distance_Difference\'] = df[\'Horizontal_Distance_To_Roadways\'] - df[\'Horizontal_Dis